DO NOT OVER-SPECIFY

This is extremely important.

Do not take a broad problem and descend into an absurdly tiny hypothetical use case just to create a "low competition" keyword.

For example:

BAD:
"PDF tool for extracting the third font appearing on page 17 of a PDF."

GOOD:
"PDF font extractor" if there is meaningful demand and weak competition.

BAD:
"Mouse test for a specific obscure gaming mouse model."

GOOD:
"Mouse double-click test" if it has meaningful demand and weak competition.

We want a NORMAL search problem with a focused solution.

The tool should be niche, not ridiculous.

