ed pages on their domain. Do NOT say: "Competitor X exists, therefore demand is validated." Instead say: "Competitor X exists, but receives almost no organic traffic, therefore this is NOT yet validated." Prefer candidates where: - multiple competitors receive organic traffic OR - one strong relevant competitor receives substantial traffic OR - the keyword cluster itself has strong measurable search demand even though current tools are weak. -------------------------------------------------- IMPORTANT DISTINCTION -------------------------------------------------- We are looking for: HIGHER-DEMAND + LOWER-COMPETITION NOT: LOW-DEMAND + ZERO-COMPETITION. Do NOT optimize for finding the most obscure possible tool. The target is a normal problem that a meaningful number of people encounter, but which has not yet attracted a large number of strong SEO competitors. Think: "100–10,000+ monthly search ecosystem with weak SERP" rather than: "50 searches and nobody has built it." -------------------------------------------------- TRAFFIC VALIDATION PRIORITY -------------------------------------------------- Rank evidence in this order: 1. Multiple relevant keywords with meaningful search volume 2. Multiple competitors receiving relevant organic traffic 3. A relevant competitor/page ranking for many related queries 4. Strong Google SERP evidence 5. Repeated user questions/forums 6. Existence of a tool alone Do NOT treat #6 as sufficient validation. DO NOT FORCE THE OUTPUT TO CONTAIN 10–15 IDEAS. Research a large pool internally, but only present candidates that genuinely pass the validation criteria. If only 2 ideas pass, give me 2. If zero pass, tell me zero passed and explain why. NEVER fill the list with weak or speculative ideas merely to reach a target number. CATEGORY FOR THIS RESEARCH: Device, Browser & Digital Diagnostics